# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ADMIN - DELETE INVARIANTS
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Verified against AdminEndpoints.Handlers.cs (DeleteMechanicAsync / ValidateMechanicDeletionInvariantsAsync):
# 403 self-delete (caller person_id claim == target id), 403 when the target carries the Admin role,
# 404 unknown id, 422 when it is the last mechanic OR would leave an appointment without any
# assignee, 409 only on a DbUpdateConcurrencyException/Postgres serialization-failure/deadlock, 200
# with body { message } (not 204) on success.
#
# No id here is hardcoded: an earlier version of this file hardcoded
# CurrentAdminMechanicId/AnotherAdminMechanicId/MechanicIdWithSoleAssignments/MechanicIdCandidateForDeletion
# as literals 6/9/7/8 and deleted id 8 on every run; as other suites created and deleted fixtures, the
# auto-increment counter drifted until id 8 pointed at the real ARSM_TEST_MECHANIC_EMAIL account,
# deleting it on every run and turning that login into a permanent 401. Every id below is either
# resolved from a same-run response or a disposable mechanic this file registers and disposes of
# itself.

@AutoService_ApiService_HostAddress = {{$processEnv AutoService_ApiService_HostAddress}}
@WebUI_Origin = {{$processEnv ARSM_TEST_WEBUI_ORIGIN}}
@AdminEmail = {{$processEnv ARSM_TEST_ADMIN_EMAIL}}
@AdminPassword = {{$processEnv ARSM_TEST_ADMIN_PASSWORD}}
@TestPassword = {{$processEnv ARSM_TEST_PASSWORD}}
@RunId = {{$timestamp}}
@UnknownMechanicId = 999999


# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### [Setup][Admin] Clear any session cookie left by a previous file (204 or 401, not asserted)
POST {{AutoService_ApiService_HostAddress}}/api/auth/logout
Origin: {{WebUI_Origin}}

###

### [Setup][Admin] Login as admin (200 expected)
# @name adminLogin
POST {{AutoService_ApiService_HostAddress}}/api/auth/login
Origin: {{WebUI_Origin}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{AdminEmail}}",
  "password": "{{AdminPassword}}"
}

{{
  exports.CsrfToken = response.headers['set-cookie']?.find(c => c.startsWith('autoservice_csrf='))?.match(/^autoservice_csrf=([^;]+)/)?.[1];
}}

?? status == 200

###

### [Negative][Admin] Admin cannot delete own account (403 expected)
# CurrentAdminMechanicId is resolved from the login response personId field (AuthEndpoints.Contracts.cs
# LoginResponse), never hardcoded, because DeleteMechanicAsync compares the caller person_id claim to
# the route id, so it must be this session own id, whichever mechanic happens to be admin.
DELETE {{AutoService_ApiService_HostAddress}}/api/admin/mechanics/{{adminLogin.personId}}
Origin: {{WebUI_Origin}}
X-CSRF-Token: {{CsrfToken}}

?? status == 403

###

# COVERAGE GAP (do not fill by mutating shared seed):
# DeleteMechanicAsync also 403s when the target mechanic carries the Admin role ("Cannot delete an
# administrator account."). The demo seed (Data/DemoDataInitializer.cs) grants the Admin role to
# exactly one mechanic, gabor.kovacs@example.com, and no API endpoint promotes another account to
# Admin - only DemoDataInitializer does that at startup. Provisioning a second admin to exercise this
# branch would require permanently mutating the shared demo seed every other suite depends on, so
# this case is documented here instead of executed (same convention as the coverage-gap comment in
# tests/API/catalog/catalog-authz.http).

# COVERAGE GAP (do not fill by mutating shared seed):
# ValidateMechanicDeletionInvariantsAsync also 422s when db.Mechanics.CountAsync() <= 1 ("Cannot
# delete the last remaining mechanic."). Reaching that state would require deleting every other
# mechanic in the shared demo database down to exactly one, which every other suite that logs in as
# a seeded mechanic depends on staying intact, so this case is documented here instead of executed.


### [Setup][Admin] Resolve a seeded customer that owns a vehicle (200 expected)
# @name seedCustomers
GET {{AutoService_ApiService_HostAddress}}/api/customers

?? status == 200

###

@SoleAssignmentCustomerId = {{seedCustomers.find(c => c.vehicleCount > 0).id}}

### [Setup][Admin] Resolve one of that customer vehicles (200 expected)
# @name seedVehicles
GET {{AutoService_ApiService_HostAddress}}/api/customers/{{SoleAssignmentCustomerId}}/vehicles

?? status == 200

###

### [Setup][Admin] Register a disposable mechanic to be an appointment sole assignee (200 expected)
# @name soleAssignmentMechanic
POST {{AutoService_ApiService_HostAddress}}/api/auth/register
Origin: {{WebUI_Origin}}
X-CSRF-Token: {{CsrfToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "Delete",
  "lastName": "SoleAssignment",
  "email": "delete.mechanic.sole.{{RunId}}@example.test",
  "password": "{{TestPassword}}",
  "personType": "Mechanic",
  "specialization": "GasolineAndDiesel",
  "expertise": ["Engine"]
}

?? status == 200

###

### [Setup][Admin] Create an appointment where the disposable mechanic is the sole assignee (201 expected)
# No DELETE /api/appointments/{id} route exists (AppointmentEndpoints.cs), so this fixture
# appointment stays on the calendar after this file runs - an accepted gap, the same as the two
# coverage gaps documented above, because the API offers no way to remove it.
# @name soleAssignmentAppt
POST {{AutoService_ApiService_HostAddress}}/api/customers/{{SoleAssignmentCustomerId}}/appointments
Origin: {{WebUI_Origin}}
X-CSRF-Token: {{CsrfToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "vehicleId": {{seedVehicles[0].id}},
  "scheduledDate": "2020-01-01T10:00:00",
  "taskDescription": "ARSM delete-invariants sole-assignment fixture",
  "mechanicIds": [{{soleAssignmentMechanic.personId}}]
}

?? status == 201

###

### [Negative][Admin] Cannot delete mechanic that would leave an appointment unassigned (422 expected)
DELETE {{AutoService_ApiService_HostAddress}}/api/admin/mechanics/{{soleAssignmentMechanic.personId}}
Origin: {{WebUI_Origin}}
X-CSRF-Token: {{CsrfToken}}

?? status == 422

###

### [Cleanup][Admin] Assign a second mechanic so the disposable one is no longer the sole assignee (200 expected)
PUT {{AutoService_ApiService_HostAddress}}/api/appointments/{{soleAssignmentAppt.id}}/assign/{{adminLogin.personId}}
Origin: {{WebUI_Origin}}
X-CSRF-Token: {{CsrfToken}}

?? status == 200

###

### [Cleanup][Admin] Delete the disposable sole-assignment mechanic now that the invariant no longer blocks it (200 expected)
DELETE {{AutoService_ApiService_HostAddress}}/api/admin/mechanics/{{soleAssignmentMechanic.personId}}
Origin: {{WebUI_Origin}}
X-CSRF-Token: {{CsrfToken}}

?? status == 200

###

### [Setup][Admin] Register a disposable mechanic with no appointment assignments (200 expected)
# @name deletableMechanic
POST {{AutoService_ApiService_HostAddress}}/api/auth/register
Origin: {{WebUI_Origin}}
X-CSRF-Token: {{CsrfToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "Delete",
  "lastName": "Candidate",
  "email": "delete.mechanic.candidate.{{RunId}}@example.test",
  "password": "{{TestPassword}}",
  "personType": "Mechanic",
  "specialization": "GasolineAndDiesel",
  "expertise": ["Engine"]
}

?? status == 200

###

### [Positive][Admin] Delete non-admin mechanic when invariants hold (200 expected)
DELETE {{AutoService_ApiService_HostAddress}}/api/admin/mechanics/{{deletableMechanic.personId}}
Origin: {{WebUI_Origin}}
X-CSRF-Token: {{CsrfToken}}

?? status == 200

###

### [Manual][Admin] Concurrent mechanic delete contention returns conflict (409 expected)
# Not automated: IsMechanicDeleteConcurrencyConflict only matches a DbUpdateConcurrencyException or a
# Postgres serialization-failure/deadlock raised while the Serializable transaction in
# DeleteMechanicAsync is in flight, which cannot be forced deterministically over plain sequential
# HTTP calls. To reproduce by hand: register a disposable mechanic, then fire two concurrent
# DELETE /api/admin/mechanics/{id} requests against it from separate admin sessions at the same time.

###

### [Manual][Admin] Linked identity delete failure returns server error (500 expected)
# Not automated: reaching this branch requires UserManager.DeleteAsync to fail for a mechanic whose
# IdentityUserId still resolves to a user, which normally cannot happen through the public API
# surface (fault-inject the Identity store, or delete the IdentityUser row directly, to reproduce by
# hand).

###

### [Negative][Admin] Cannot delete unknown mechanic (404 expected)
DELETE {{AutoService_ApiService_HostAddress}}/api/admin/mechanics/{{UnknownMechanicId}}
Origin: {{WebUI_Origin}}
X-CSRF-Token: {{CsrfToken}}

?? status == 404
